      {
        "id": "story",
        "type": "story",
        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "Train timetable"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "A train ticket says 17:30. Is that morning or evening? The 24-hour clock tells us exactly, with no a.m. or p.m. Let us learn to convert."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "24-hour",
          "a.m. and p.m.",
          "a.m. same",
          "match",
          "p.m. add 12",
          "subtract 12"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "In the 12-hour format we write a.m. for the time from midnight to noon and p.m. for noon to midnight.\nThe 24-hour format counts the hours from 00:00 to 24:00 and has no a.m. or p.m.\nFor a.m. times the hour digits stay the same. 05:30 a.m. is 05:30 hours and 11:55 a.m. is 11:55 hours.\nFor p.m. times add 12 to the hour. 02:30 p.m. is 14:30 hours; 05:30 p.m. is 17:30 hours; 09:35 p.m. is 21:35 hours.\nTo go back, subtract 12: 20:45 hours is 08:45 p.m., and 23:45 hours is 11:45 p.m.\nMatch examples from the book: 06:30 a.m. = 06:30, 04:30 a.m. = 04:30, 01:30 a.m. = 01:30, 07:30 p.m. = 19:30, 08:45 p.m. = 20:45, 11:45 p.m. = 23:45."
        }
      },
